  "recordedAt": "2026-05-07T15:00:00Z",
  "contextText": "Revisiting where the pilot runs after the pricing came in.",
  "hasTranscript": true,
  "speakers": [
    {
      "id": "m18-spk-a",
      "label": "A",
      "displayName": "Alma Mockwell"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-spk-b",
      "label": "B",
      "displayName": "Pia Sample"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-spk-c",
      "label": "C",
      "displayName": "Jovan Démo"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-spk-d",
      "label": "D",
      "displayName": "Otis Dummyson"
    }
  ],
  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "m18-s001",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 0,
      "endMs": 6300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thanks for joining, Otis. We need to revisit the hosting decision we made in February."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s002",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-b",
      "startMs": 6550,
      "endMs": 14750,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The committed-use pricing from Estuary finally came in, and it's about 40 percent above the budget we agreed with Lambda."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s003",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-d",
      "startMs": 15000,
      "endMs": 23200,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "That's a non-starter for us. And honestly, since I joined we've built out an on-prem cluster that's sitting half empty."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s004",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-c",
      "startMs": 23450,
      "endMs": 32410,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I've looked at it. It has everything the pilot needs, and the floor data never leaves Lambda's network, which security will love."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s005",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 32660,
      "endMs": 35920,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "What would it cost us to move?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s006",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-c",
      "startMs": 36170,
      "endMs": 40950,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "The services are containerised already. JD's estimate, three weeks including testing."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s007",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-b",
      "startMs": 41200,
      "endMs": 44460,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "And we'd avoid the Estuary contract entirely."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s008",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-d",
      "startMs": 44710,
      "endMs": 51390,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "From my side, I'd rather the pilot runs on our cluster anyway. My team supports it."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s009",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 51640,
      "endMs": 59460,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Then I think we reverse the February decision. The pilot moves off Estuary Cloud to Lambda's own on-prem cluster."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s010",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-b",
      "startMs": 59710,
      "endMs": 60690,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s011",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-d",
      "startMs": 60940,
      "endMs": 61920,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Agreed."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s012",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 62170,
      "endMs": 64290,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "JD, what's the plan?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s013",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-c",
      "startMs": 64540,
      "endMs": 69700,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll migrate the pilot services to the Lambda cluster by May 29."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s014",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-d",
      "startMs": 69950,
      "endMs": 74350,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "My team will give you namespaces and access by Monday."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s015",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 74600,
      "endMs": 78240,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Pia, can you let Thane at Estuary know?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s016",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-b",
      "startMs": 78490,
      "endMs": 85170,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Yes, I'll tell Thane this week. He was helpful, so I want to do it properly."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s017",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 85420,
      "endMs": 88300,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Good. Anything else for the move?"
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s018",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-c",
      "startMs": 88550,
      "endMs": 92570,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Monitoring. We need to plug into your existing dashboards."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s019",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-d",
      "startMs": 92820,
      "endMs": 97600,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "I'll set JD up with read access to our monitoring stack."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s020",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 97850,
      "endMs": 104150,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Great. Unrelated, for the go-live lunch, JD's vegetarian, so let's not do the barbecue place."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s021",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-c",
      "startMs": 104400,
      "endMs": 106140,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Thank you, yes."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18-s022",
      "speakerId": "m18-spk-a",
      "startMs": 106390,
      "endMs": 110410,
      "rev": 1,
      "text": "Okay, that's it. Off Estuary, on-prem by May 29."
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "version": 1,
    "body": "# Pilot hosting decision revisited\n\n**Date:** May 7\n**Attendees:** Alma Mockwell (Larkspur Labs), Pia Sample (Larkspur Labs), JD (Larkspur Labs), Otis Dummyson (Org Lambda Robotics)\n\n## Summary\n\nThe team revisited February's hosting decision for the Lambda pick-path pilot after Estuary Cloud's committed-use pricing arrived.\n\n## Discussion\n\n- Estuary's pricing came in about 40 percent above the budget agreed with Lambda. Otis called it a non-starter.\n- Since Otis joined, Lambda has built out an on-prem cluster that is half empty. JD has reviewed it: it has everything the pilot needs, and floor data would never leave Lambda's network.\n- The services are already containerised; JD estimates three weeks to move, including testing.\n- Otis's team supports the cluster and would rather the pilot runs there.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- **Reverse the February decision.** The pilot moves off Estuary Cloud to **Lambda's own on-prem cluster**, avoiding the Estuary contract entirely.\n\n## Action items\n\n- **JD** — migrate the pilot services to the Lambda cluster by May 29.\n- **Otis Dummyson** — provide namespaces and access by Monday, and read access to the monitoring stack for JD.\n- **Pia Sample** — tell Thane at Estuary about the change this week.\n\n## Notes\n\n- For the go-live lunch, choose a place with good vegetarian options.\n"
  },
